# Force LF on checkout for every text file, on every platform. Without `eol=lf`, `* text=auto` writes the
# platform-native ending on checkout, so a Windows checkout gets CRLF in 322 of the skill files even with
# core.autocrlf=false; a consumer that vendors the skills by copying that checkout then commits CRLF (#129,
# ADR-0090). The repo's blobs are already LF; this only changes what a working-tree checkout receives.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.mjs text
# Shell scripts must check out with LF even on Windows, or the bash that runs them
# (CI and the ADR/ruleset gate tests) fails on CR bytes (`$'\r': command not found`).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Append-only logs (the skill-application receipt log, the arch-review log) get ONE new line per PR,
# always at the end. Two PRs open at once therefore collide on that last line every time. `merge=union`
# is git's built-in driver for exactly this: on a merge it keeps BOTH sides' added lines instead of
# raising a conflict, so append-only logs never block a PR. It is safe here precisely because these
# files are append-only (no line is ever edited in place, so there is nothing to mis-merge). GitHub
# honors this driver when it merges, so the conflicts stop at the source, not just locally.
# Any file named log.jsonl, in any directory, is one of these logs.
log.jsonl merge=union

# The changelog is the third file every PR edits: each PR adds a "### Fixed (...)" block near the top, so
# two open PRs collide there the same way the logs do (ADR-0087). It only ever gains new blocks (existing
# entries are not rewritten), so the same union driver is the right fix: a merge keeps both PRs' new
# entries instead of raising a conflict. union is NEVER applied to source code, only to these accumulating
# text files, because concatenating both sides of a code conflict can produce wrong code.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# The pre-push hook template is a shebang script; it must check out with LF so it runs under the shell
# that git invokes it with, even on Windows.
.claude/skills/bootstrap/templates/pre-push text eol=lf

# This repo's OWN armed hooks (self-dogfood, ADR-0053) are shebang scripts git invokes directly, so they
# must check out with LF even on Windows or the shell fails on the CR bytes.
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf
.githooks/install-hooks.mjs text eol=lf
.claude/skills/bootstrap/templates/install-hooks.mjs text eol=lf
